1. What do all the methods (move(), special_move(), use()) in the previous activities have in common?

They have the same purpose of performing an action, but each class gives them a different behavior.

2. How does this activity show polymorphism in a gaming context?

It shows polymorphism because different characters and items can perform different actions using the same method.

3. Can you think of other examples where the same action behaves differently depending on the character or item?

Yes. A healing item restores health, while a shield protects the player. Different characters can also have different attack abilities.
